  (branch `master`).

Four files under `bolt12/` are test-vector sources for this module; two are
vendored as generated Zig data files, two are reproduced as inline hex
literals directly in `bolt12.zig`'s own test bodies (a pre-existing style
this pass did not change):

  * `bolt12/offers-test.json` (53 rows, ALL vendored verbatim) —
    transcribed mechanically (never hand-typed) into
    `src/bolt12_offers_kat_vectors.zig`; each row's `description`/`valid`/
    `bolt12`/`fields` is reproduced byte-exact. Driven by `bolt12.zig`'s
    "BOLT#12 KAT: offer ENCODE ..." / "... offer DECODE ..." tests (all 20
    `"valid": true` rows plus the 2 `"valid": false` rows whose TLV bytes
    are still wire-well-formed — 22 of 53 rows carry a `fields` breakdown to
    drive ENCODE/DECODE against) and by 12 targeted rejection tests for the
    remaining wire-malformed rows. The other 21 `"valid": false` rows
    exercise checks this module does not implement (UTF-8 validation,
    blinded-path internal structure, curve-point validity, feature-bit
    semantics, reader "MUST NOT respond" business policy) — listed
    individually, with the BOLT#12 reasoning for each, in the comment block
    immediately preceding `bolt12.zig`'s Merkle/signature test section.

  * `bolt12/format-string-test.json` (12 rows, ALL vendored verbatim) —
    transcribed mechanically into `src/bolt12_format_string_kat_vectors.zig`;
    drives `bech32_raw.stripContinuation`/`splitHrp`'s `+`-continuation and
    upper/lowercase acceptance rules end-to-end through `decodeOffer`.

  * `bolt12/signature-test.json` — NOT vendored as a separate file; specific
    hex values (the `n1` 1/2/3-leaf Merkle-root test TLVs, and the full
    `invoice_request` worked example: Alice/Bob's offer fields, the 6-leaf
    Merkle root, and the BIP-340 signature) are reproduced as inline hex
    string literals directly in `bolt12.zig`'s own "BOLT#12 KAT: n1 Merkle
    roots" / "BOLT#12 KAT: invoice_request Merkle root + signature verify"
    tests, predating this pass.

  * `bolt12/payer-proof-test.json` — likewise not vendored separately; the
    `"full_disclosure"` vector's raw `invoice_hex` TLV stream, Merkle root,
    and `invoice_signature` are reproduced as inline hex literals in
    `bolt12.zig`'s "BOLT#12 KAT: invoice Merkle root + signature verify"
    test, predating this pass.

A fifth file, `bolt12/format-string-test.json`'s sibling
`bootstrap.bolt12.org`-hosted vector set, was never fetched or used: that
hostname is NXDOMAIN and was the reason `ANCHOR-TASKS.tsv` previously marked
this module BLOCKED. It was never needed — the official vectors live in
`lightning/bolts` (this file's own source), reachable without it.

Implementation vs. test-data distinction: the BOLT#11/BOLT#12 wire-format
CODEC and Merkle/BIP-340 signature machinery in `bolt11.zig`/`bolt12.zig` are
this module's own clean-room work from the public spec text (`11-payment-
encoding.md` / `12-offer-encoding.md`) — that needs no attribution per root
`NOTICE` §0 (a public spec is not a copyrightable work). What is reproduced
here, and only here, is the SPECIFICATION AUTHORS' OWN TEST-CASE DATA, which
is precisely why this notice exists and lives beside it rather than in root
`NOTICE` (per root `NOTICE` §1's policy: attribution for reproduced
third-party data travels with the module that owes it).
